  extracted as `Inn(A_F) / Z(A_F)` where `Inn(A_F)` is generated by
  unitary elements `u` satisfying `u* · u = 1` (i.e., `‖u‖² = 1`
  in the canonical norm).

  This file ships the SQUARED-NORM function on the c_part field,
  the foundation step before introducing `IsUnitary` in a future
  iteration.  Component-wise, the c_part is `ℂ ≅ ℝ × ℝ`, and the
  natural norm is the standard Euclidean modulus.

